menu "Stream C I/O"

if LIBC_LZF

config STREAM_LZF_BLOG
	int "Log2 of block size"
	default 10
	range 9 12
	---help---
		This stream uses two buffers of size a little more than
		(1 << CONFIG_STREAM_LZF_BLOG) to compress and decompress data in
		chunks. Slightly better compression should be obtainable with larger

		NOTE:  This is a pairing option for using the decompression tool,
		       chunks must match with compression

endif

config STREAM_BSPRINTF_EMBED_FORMAT
	bool "Self-contained bsprintf records"
	default DRIVERS_NOTERPMSG
	---help---
		Make lib_bsprintf() store the format string in the record itself,
		prefixed by the name of the image that packed it, instead of leaving
		the format string to be addressed by the reader:

			[prefix\0][fmt\0][arguments...]

		The address of a format string is meaningful just inside the image
		that packed the record, so a reader living anywhere else faults or
		prints garbage when it resolves that address. This happens whenever
		the reader is not the producer:

		- Another core reads the records forwarded by the noterpmsg driver.
		- Another image reads a note buffer that survived a warm restart,
		  where DRIVERS_NOTERAM_SECTION points at retained memory: a boot
		  stage (bootloader, OTA, recovery) packs a record and the image it
		  jumps to unpacks it.

		Enable this on such short lived images. Leave it disabled on images
		that use these records for high rate tracing, where the extra copy
		and the larger records do matter.

		The arguments are then always packed by parsing the format string, so
		the encoding no longer depends on the type word the caller derived at
		compile time, that is on DRIVERS_NOTE_STRIP_FORMAT for a note.

		Set STREAM_BSPRINTF_PREFIX to name the image, or the records are
		reported without a source name.

config STREAM_BSPRINTF_PREFIX
	string "Name of the image packing bsprintf records"
	depends on STREAM_BSPRINTF_EMBED_FORMAT
	default RPMSG_LOCAL_CPUNAME if RPMSG
	default LIBC_HOSTNAME if !RPMSG
	---help---
		Name of the image that packed a record, stored in the record and
		reported as a [prefix] tag when it is unpacked. Use something that
		identifies the producer to whoever reads the records: the core for a
		cross core reader ("ap", "cp"), the boot stage for an image that
		inherits a retained buffer ("ota", "recovery").

		Defaults to RPMSG_LOCAL_CPUNAME where there is rpmsg, which is what
		the noterpmsg driver used to store on its own. Leave it empty to keep
		self-contained records without naming their source.

config STREAM_OUT_BUFFER_SIZE
	int "Output stream buffer size"
	default 64

config STREAM_HEXDUMP_BUFFER_SIZE
	int "Output hexdump stream buffer size"
	default 128

config STREAM_BASE64_BUFFER_SIZE
	int "Output base64 stream buffer size"
	default 128

endmenu # Locale Support
